Upstream review, 2026-10-09
--------------------------

RTK v0.51.0, commit e001f773f80b22b7dc4c7a79521b30e35aaef026:
https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk/releases/tag/v0.51.0
Adopted the output-size guard, recovery of original output before filtering,
graceful recovery-storage failure, terminal-style cleanup, preservation of
explicit output formats, and shell argument boundary safeguards. pi-rs uses
exclusive, private recovery files to avoid overwriting concurrent output.
The SQLite recall/history service and additional tool-specific wrappers were
not adopted: they require new persistence and CLI contracts beyond this
standalone toolbox's existing recovery-file interface.

oh-my-pi commit 703a261df9533e74f16aa8d38e64eb41977ccf89:
https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/tree/703a261df9533e74f16aa8d38e64eb41977ccf89/crates/pi-ast
Adapted breadth-first summary unfolding, JSON-pair pattern contexts, and
linear edit application with identical-edit deduplication and UTF-8 range
validation. pi-rs retains its embedded grammar set: upstream's runtime WASM
grammar distribution and process-wide parse cache are designed for its
long-running application, while pi-rs runs a standalone command per request.

Grammar compatibility patches
-----------------------------

vendor/tree-sitter-clojure is crates.io tree-sitter-clojure 0.1.0,
source commit 6248a3f3d3c76ec7d33c52e7553761facdcb4ab5 (MIT wrapper;
the included Clojure grammar's COPYING.txt is retained).
vendor/tree-sitter-just is crates.io tree-sitter-just 0.2.0,
source commit 5685543a6e64f66335e25518c9ae8ffa1dae3d01 (MIT, LICENSE retained).
Only the normalized Cargo manifests are patched: tree-sitter is moved from
dependencies to dev-dependencies and updated to 0.27. Both libraries expose
LanguageFn and use the runtime only in examples/tests. This permits the
current ast-grep/Tree-sitter stack without changing either parser. The
original manifests and source revision metadata are preserved for review.

The yanked tree-sitter-perl-next package is replaced by the maintained
ts-parser-perl 2.0 grammar from https://github.com/tree-sitter-perl/tree-sitter-perl.

vendor/tree-sitter-sequel is crates.io tree-sitter-sequel 0.3.11,
source revision metadata 7b51ecda191d36b92f5a90a8d1bc3faef1c7b8b8 (marked
"dirty" by the publisher). Its parser and scanner are byte-identical to the
published crate. Only the normalized manifest changes cc from ~1.2.1 to 1.6.
The upstream MIT LICENSE was recovered from that revision because the
published crate omitted it. Cargo.toml.orig and .cargo_vcs_info.json are retained.

All 78 direct registry dependencies were checked against current stable
crates.io releases on 2026-10-09. Cargo.lock records the resolved versions,
including cc 1.6.0. A separate version-by-version audit of all 232 locked
registry entries found six required older major lines: getrandom 0.2.17
(const-random-macro), syn 2.0.119 (phf_macros/tracing-attributes), r-efi 6.0.0
(getrandom/UEFI), redox_syscall 0.5.18 (parking_lot_core/Redox), wasi
0.11.1+wasi-snapshot-preview1 (getrandom/WASI), and windows-link 0.2.1
(parking_lot_core/windows-sys/Windows). These are current compatible releases
within upstream constraints; newer majors also coexist where required. Rust 1.99.0 (2026-10-01 stable) is pinned in the root
rust-toolchain.toml and provided by rust-overlay to development and builds.

Comparison-driven changes, pi-rs 0.3.0
--------------------------------------

Independent implementations informed by the native/pi-rs/RTK comparison:
selective inline guidance, plain CLI search/summary, complete pagination,
byte budgets and targeted reads, timestamp-aware logs, conservative test
summaries, complete history capture, compact diff evidence, JSON pointers and
heterogeneous shapes, chronological pipes and explicit native streaming,
content-addressed gzip recovery with bounded retention. The historical
comparison and the fresh verification report remain in the parent reports/.
